{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Stat Engine API",
    "description": "Normalized, source-agnostic sports data API. Major competition coverage includes NBA, MLB, NFL, NHL, KBO, NCAA (basketball and football), and soccer competitions such as EPL, La Liga, Bundesliga, Serie A, Ligue 1, UCL, MLS, and FIFA tournaments.\n\nThe complete canonical sport identifiers understood by the API are: `basketball`, `football`, `baseball`, `hockey`, `soccer`, `golf`, `tennis`, `racing`, `mma`, `lacrosse`, `rugby`, `volleyball`, `australian_football`, `rugby_league`, `water_polo`, and `field_hockey`. These identifiers describe data shape; call `GET /v1/competitions` for the currently registered competition slugs and `GET /v1/competitions/{comp}/capabilities` for the phases, measures, and standings tables available for a particular competition.\n\nCore resources — persons, teams, competitions/editions, contests, and entrants — carry minted ids that serialize as `<prefix>_<base32>` (`per_`, `team_`, `comp_`, `edt_`, `game_`, `cst_`, `ent_`); the prefix is part of the type. Stats are typed per-phase and reconstruct as-of any ingested instant from appearance facts.\n\n## Endpoint groups\n\n| Group | Base path | Description |\n|-------|-----------|-------------|\n| Persons | `/v1/persons` | Profile, appearances, game log, memberships, season stats, per-person capability discovery, composed player overview |\n| Teams | `/v1/teams` | Profile, as-of roster, games, game log, season stats |\n| Competitions | `/v1/competitions` | Competitions, editions, edition participants/games/standings, capability discovery |\n| Contests | `/v1/contests` | Generalized contest detail for team matches, individual matches, and field/N-ary events; team-match boxscores and sport-scoped play-by-play where available |\n| Analysis | `/v1/analysis` | Player-prop card and team comparison (all plans; metered at analysis weights) |\n| Account | `/v1/account` | Authenticated plan usage (unmetered — checking quota never consumes units) |\n| Assets | `/v1/assets` | Team logo PNGs (proxied, 7-day cache) |\n\n## Authentication\n\nAll endpoints in this spec require an API key passed in the `X-API-Key` request header.\n\n## Operational endpoints\n\nLiveness/readiness probes (`/healthz`, `/readyz`, `/metrics`) and ingest administration endpoints (`/v1/ingest/...`) are intentionally **not documented in this spec**. They are operator-only surfaces and live in a separate internal spec; see infra docs for access.\n\n## Response envelope\n\nEvery response wraps its payload in:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"data\": {... },\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"request_id\": \"uuid\",\n    \"source\": \"source identifier\",\n    \"fetched_at\": \"2025-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\n    \"cache\": \"HIT | MISS | STALE\",\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nError responses use `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`.\n`meta.request_id` uniquely identifies the request — quote it when filing support tickets. `meta.cache` is reserved for response-layer caching (`HIT` / `STALE` / `MISS`); entity reads are currently served directly from the canonical store and always report `MISS`.\n\n## Freshness\n\nReads are served from the canonical store, which ingest refreshes out-of-band on a per-resource cadence:\n\n- **Live box scores** are re-ingested within minutes of in-game updates while a slate is live.\n- **Standings** are recomputed whenever a game in the edition finalizes.\n- **Schedules** are re-synced several times per day.\n- **Final box scores** are immutable once a game is final.\n\n`meta.fetched_at` reports when the response was assembled, not when the underlying data last changed upstream.\n\n## Capability discovery\n\nCall `GET /v1/competitions/{comp}/capabilities` to retrieve the exact stat keys (base + derived measures) each phase reports for a competition's sport.\n\nCall `GET /v1/persons/{person_id}/capabilities?competition=&season=` to retrieve only the phases (and their stat keys) a specific person **actually recorded data for** that season — a presence-filtered projection of the same registry, so you never have to probe `/stats` to learn which props a player can settle.\n\n## Versioning and deprecation\n\nEvery endpoint lives under a major-version URL path prefix (`/v1/…`). Changes within a major version are additive only (new endpoints, optional parameters, response fields, competitions, stat keys, error codes); clients must ignore unknown fields. Breaking changes ship as a new major path (`/v2/…`) served alongside the old one. Documented exception: the 2026-09-11 paid self-serve quota hard-stop changed at-cap metered `/v1` responses from `200` to `429 QUOTA_EXCEEDED` without a new major path; see the changelog. Deprecations are announced with `Deprecation` (RFC 9745) and `Sunset` (RFC 8594) response headers on the affected operation, `deprecated: true` in this document, and a dated changelog entry — at least 90 days before sunset for an operation and 12 months for a whole major version. Full policy: https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/versioning\n\n## Permissions and scopes\n\nThe REST API is read-only: an API key can read data and consume quota, never write data or manage the account. Keys come in two environments, `sk_live_…` and `sk_test_…`, so traffic classes can be rotated and audited independently; create one key per integration. All plans include every endpoint, including `/v1/analysis/*`. The MCP server uses OAuth 2.1 scopes `stats:read` and `analysis:read`. Details: https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/permissions\n\n## Rate limits and errors\n\nEvery metered response carries `X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, and `X-RateLimit-Reset` (per-second GCRA limiter, per account); monthly quota is reported in `X-Account-Quota-*`. A `429` carries `Retry-After` and an `error.code` of `RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` or `QUOTA_EXCEEDED`. All errors share the typed `ErrorResponse` shape `{\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}}` and every response carries `X-Request-Id`. Rate limits: https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/rate-limits · Error codes: https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/error-codes",
    "license": {
      "name": ""
    },
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "contact": {
      "name": "statshawk support",
      "email": "support@statshawk.ai",
      "url": "https://statshawk.ai/contact"
    },
    "termsOfService": "https://statshawk.ai/terms",
    "x-versioning": {
      "strategy": "url-path",
      "current": "v1",
      "compatibility": "additive-only within a major version, except documented changelog exceptions (2026-09-11 quota hard-stop under /v1)",
      "policy": "https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/versioning"
    },
    "x-deprecation-policy": {
      "headers": [
        "Deprecation",
        "Sunset"
      ],
      "minimumNoticeDays": 90,
      "majorVersionRetirementMonths": 12,
      "changelog": "https://statshawk.ai/docs/changelog",
      "policy": "https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/versioning"
    },
    "x-permissions": {
      "access": "read-only",
      "apiKeyEnvironments": [
        "sk_live_",
        "sk_test_"
      ],
      "mcpOAuthScopes": [
        "stats:read",
        "analysis:read"
      ],
      "policy": "https://statshawk.ai/docs/getting-started/permissions"
    }
  },
  "paths": {
    "/v1/account/usage": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Account"
        ],
        "summary": "GET /v1/account/usage — current plan, period usage, and analysis access.",
        "description": "Unmetered by design. A valid credential always receives 200, including\nwhen the account is already over its hard cap.",
        "operationId": "get_v1_account_usage",
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Current-period plan usage (unmetered; does not consume quota)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponseAccountUsage"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Missing or invalid API key",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limit (`RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`) or monthly quota (`QUOTA_EXCEEDED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              },
              "Retry-After": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/Retry-After"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Account store unavailable or quota ledger read failed",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "501": {
            "description": "Capability not supported for this competition (`NOT_SUPPORTED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "Upstream data provider failed (`PROVIDER_ERROR`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Database connection pool unavailable",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "/v1/analysis/compare-teams": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Analysis"
        ],
        "summary": "GET /v1/analysis/compare-teams?a=&b=&as_of= — clubs OR national teams.",
        "operationId": "get_v1_analysis_compare_teams",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "a",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Team A (minted id). Required.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TeamId"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "b",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Team B (minted id). Required.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/TeamId"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "season",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Season start year — roster of persons who appeared that season.\nCross-year leagues (NBA/NHL/NCAA) use the year the season STARTS in\n(2025 = the 2025-26 season).",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "null"
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SeasonYear"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "as_of",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "RFC3339 instant — who represented the team in a window ending here.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "date-time"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "edition",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Tournament edition id — appearances ∪ edition-overlapping memberships.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "null"
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EditionId"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "days",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Look-back window in days for the `Current`/`AsOf` scopes (clamped `[1, 90]`).",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "integer",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "int32"
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "Two teams and their as-of rosters laid side by side (clubs or national sides)",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponseTeamComparison"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "`a` and `b` (team ids) are required",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Missing or invalid API key (`UNAUTHORIZED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "404": {
            "description": "One of the team ids names no team",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "429": {
            "description": "Rate limit (`RATE_LIMIT_EXCEEDED`) or monthly quota (`QUOTA_EXCEEDED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              },
              "Retry-After": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/Retry-After"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "500": {
            "description": "Internal failure (`INTERNAL_ERROR`, `CACHE_ERROR`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "501": {
            "description": "Capability not supported for this competition (`NOT_SUPPORTED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "502": {
            "description": "Upstream data provider failed (`PROVIDER_ERROR`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "503": {
            "description": "Auth backend, DB, or providers unavailable (`AUTH_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE`, `DB_UNAVAILABLE`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "x-requires-tier": "any",
        "x-statshawk-weight-class": "analysis",
        "x-statshawk-weight": 10
      }
    },
    "/v1/analysis/player-prop": {
      "get": {
        "tags": [
          "Analysis"
        ],
        "summary": "GET /v1/analysis/player-prop?person_id=&stat=&line= — person-keyed.",
        "operationId": "get_v1_analysis_player_prop",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "person_id",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "The person to analyse (minted `per_…` id). Required.",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PersonId"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "stat",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "The measure to analyse. Required. May be **phase-qualified** as\n`phase.measure` (e.g. `pitching.so`, `passing.yards`) to disambiguate a\nmeasure that exists in more than one phase — this is the canonical\nform; a bare `so` matches the first phase that carries it. A curated\nset of friendly aliases is also accepted (e.g. `pitcher_k`, a baseball\ntwo-way disambiguator that resolves to `pitching.so`) — see\n[`crate::stats::measure::resolve_stat_alias`].",
            "required": true,
            "schema": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "line",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "number",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "double"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "competition",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Competition slug (e.g. `mlb`) or minted `comp_…` id. When supplied and\n`season`/`edition`/`from`/`to` are all omitted, the window defaults to\nthis competition's latest edition with at least one final contest rather\nthan every edition ever ingested.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "season",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Restrict to one season start year — cross-year leagues (NBA/NHL/NCAA)\nuse the year the season STARTS in (2025 = the 2025-26 season).\nSupplying this opts out of the default edition window.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "null"
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/SeasonYear"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "edition",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Restrict to one edition. Supplying this opts out of the\ndefault edition window.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "null"
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/EditionId"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "from",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Lower bound (inclusive) on game kickoff. Supplying this opts out of\nthe default edition window.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "date-time"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "to",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Upper bound (inclusive) on game kickoff. Supplying this opts out of\nthe default edition window.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "format": "date-time"
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "stage",
            "in": "query",
            "description": "Contest-stage filter. Omitted defaults to regular-season\n(plus unknown-stage) appearances only — the same window the season\nfold uses. `stage=all` removes the filter entirely (every stage,\nincluding preseason/exhibition/allstar); an explicit stage\n(`preseason`/`regular`/`postseason`/`exhibition`/`allstar`) narrows to\nexactly that value. An unrecognized value is a `400`.",
            "required": false,
            "schema": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "null"
                },
                {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StageSelector"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ],
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The person-keyed prop card — a context-rich per-game log, windowed averages, and (when `line` is supplied) windowed over-rates. When `competition` is given and `season`/`edition`/`from`/`to` are all omitted, the window defaults to the latest edition with at least one final contest, not every edition ever ingested",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ApiResponsePlayerPropCard"
                }
              }
            },
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "description": "`person_id` is required",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ErrorResponse"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "401": {
            "description": "Missing or invalid API key (`UNAUTHORIZED`).",
            "headers": {
              "X-Request-Id": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-Request-Id"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Limit": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Limit"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Remaining": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Remaining"
              },
              "X-RateLimit-Reset": {
                "$ref": "#/components/headers/X-RateLimit-Reset"
              }
            },
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
